  {
    "id" : "full-text",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Performance",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Use of Full Text Predicate",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of full text predicates in SQL queries to prevent performance issues.",
    "explanation" : "# Disallows use of Full Text\n\n## Rule Details\n\nUse of improperly tuned full text queries can lead to performance problems\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT Name, ListPrice\nFROM Production.Product\nWHERE ListPrice = 80.99\n   AND CONTAINS(Name, 'Mountain')\nGO\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT Name, ListPrice\nFROM Production.Product\nWHERE ListPrice = 80.99\n   AND Name like '%Mountain%'\nGO\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "information-schema",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Use of SYS.Partitions Instead of INFORMATION_SCHEMA Views",
    "description" : "This rule enforces the use of SYS.OBJECTS system views instead of INFORMATION_SCHEMA views for retrieving object metadata in T-SQL.",
    "explanation" : "# Disallows use of INFORMATION_SCHEMA views\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThe INFORMATION_SCHEMA are not the best source for object metadata, use SYS.OBJECTS\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT table_name FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES\nWHERE table_schema = 'MyTable'\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT name\nFROM sys.objects\nWHERE OBJECTPROPERTY(object_id, N'SchemaId') = SCHEMA_ID(N'Production')\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "keyword-capitalization",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Capitalization of TSQL Keywords",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that all TSQL keywords are written in uppercase to improve readability.",
    "explanation" : "# Requires use of capitalized keywords\n\n## Rule Details\n\nCapitalizing SQL keywords enhances readability and provides a clear seperation between keywords and objects\n\n```tsql\nselect * from foo;\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT * FROM foo;\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 1,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "linked-server",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Performance",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Linked Server Queries",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of linked server queries in T-SQL because they can cause table locking issues and are discouraged.",
    "explanation" : "# Disallows use of linked server calls\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule disallows linked server queries, which can cause table locking and are discouraged\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT Foo\nFROM MyServer.MyDatabase.MySchema.MyTable;\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT Foo\nFROM MyDatabase.MySchema.MyTable;\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "multi-table-alias",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Aliasing in Multi-Table Joins",
    "description" : "This rule enforces the use of table aliases when multiple tables are joined in a query to improve clarity and prevent ambiguity.",
    "explanation" : "# Enforce aliasing in multi-table joins\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule enforces the use of table aliases\nwhen multiple tables are joined in a query.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT user_name, country_name\nFROM dbo.MyTable\n    INNER JOIN dbo.Country ON id = country_id;\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT mt.user_name, c.country_name\nFROM dbo.MyTable AS mt\n    INNER JOIN dbo.Country AS c ON c.id = mt.country_id;\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "named-constraint",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Named Constraints in Temporary Tables",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of named constraints on temporary tables to prevent collisions when executed in parallel.",
    "explanation" : "# Disallows named constraints in temp tables\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule disallows named constraints in temporary tables, which can cause collisions when used in parallel.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nCREATE TABLE #temporary (\n    ID INT IDENTITY (1,1),\n    CreatedOn DATETIME2 NOT NULL\n        CONSTRAINT [df_CreatedOn] DEFAULT GETDATE());\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nCREATE TABLE #temporary (\n    ID INT IDENTITY (1,1),\n    CreatedOn DATETIME2 NOT NULL DEFAULT GETDATE());\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "non-sargable",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "Performance",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Functions on Filter Clauses or Join Predicates to Maintain SARGability",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of functions on filter clauses and join predicates in SQL queries to prevent performance degradation caused by non-SARGable conditions.",
    "explanation" : "# Disallow functions on filter clauses or join predicates\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule disallows the use of functions on filter clauses\nand join predicates, which can negatively impact performance\nby making a query non-SARGable (Search ARGumentable).\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT user_name\nFROM dbo.MyTable\nWHERE DATEDIFF(day, created_on, GETDATE()) <= 3;\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT user_name\nFROM dbo.MyTable\nWHERE created_on >= DATEADD(day, -3, GETDATE());\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 10,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "object-property",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Using ObjectProperty Function Over sys Views",
    "description" : "This rule disallows using the ObjectProperty function when a sys view could be used instead in T-SQL code.",
    "explanation" : "# Disallow using ObjectedProperty function over sys view\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule disallows using the `ObjectProperty` function\nwhen a sys view could be used instead.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nIF OBJECTPROPERTY(OBJECT_ID(N'dbo.MyTable'),'ISTABLE') = 1\nBEGIN\n   SELECT 'dbo.MyTable is a table';\nEND\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nIF EXISTS (SELECT * FROM sys.tables WHERE name = 'MyTable')\nBEGIN\n   SELECT 'dbo.MyTable is a table';\nEND\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "print-statement",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow PRINT Statements",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of PRINT statements in T-SQL code.",
    "explanation" : "# Disallow using PRINT statements\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule disallows using `PRINT` statements.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nPRINT 'This is a debug message.'\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nRAISERROR('This is a debug message.', 160, 1);\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "schema-qualify",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Schema Qualification of Object Names",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that references to database objects are qualified with their schema names.",
    "explanation" : "# Enforce qualifying objects with schema name\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule enforces qualifying references to objects with\nschema names.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT user_name\nFROM MyTable;\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT user_name\nFROM dbo.MyTable;\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "select-star",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow SELECT *",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of the asterisk (*) to select all columns in a SQL SELECT statement.",
    "explanation" : "# Disallow selecting all columns with asterisk\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule disallows selecting all columns of a table\nby using an asterisk.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT *\nFROM dbo.MyTable;\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT user_id, user_name, created_on\nFROM dbo.MyTable;\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "semicolon-termination",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Statement Termination with Semicolon",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that all Transact-SQL statements are terminated with a semicolon.",
    "explanation" : "# Enforce terminating queries with semicolons\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule enforces termination of all queries with\na semicolon, as defined by Microsoft's\n[Transact-SQL Syntax Conventions](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/t-sql/language-elements/transact-sql-syntax-conventions-transact-sql?view=sql-server-ver15)\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT user_name\nFROM dbo.MyTable\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT user_name\nFROM dbo.MyTable;\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 1,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "set-ansi",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce SET ANSI_NULLS ON Near Top of File",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that the statement SET ANSI_NULLS ON is set near the top of a T-SQL file.",
    "explanation" : "# Enforce setting SET ANSI_NULLS ON near top of file\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule enforces setting `SET ANSI_NULLS ON`\nnear the top of the file.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nDECLARE @MyVar VARCHAR(30);\nSELECT @MyVar = 'This is incorrect.';\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSET ANSI_NULLS ON;\nGO\n\nDECLARE @MyVar VARCHAR(30);\nSELECT @MyVar = 'This is correct.';\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "set-nocount",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce SET NOCOUNT ON Near Top of File",
    "description" : "Ensure that SET NOCOUNT ON is set near the top of SQL files to prevent extra result sets from interfering with output.",
    "explanation" : "# Enforce setting SET NOCOUNT ON near top of file\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule enforces setting `SET NOCOUNT ON`\nnear the top of the file.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nDECLARE @MyVar VARCHAR(30);\nSELECT @MyVar = 'This is incorrect.';\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSET NOCOUNT ON;\n\nDECLARE @MyVar VARCHAR(30);\nSELECT @MyVar = 'This is correct.';\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "set-quoted-identifier",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Compatibility",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce SET QUOTED_IDENTIFIER ON near top of file",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that the statement SET QUOTED_IDENTIFIER ON is set near the top of a T-SQL file.",
    "explanation" : "# Enforce setting SET QUOTED_IDENTIFIER ON near top of file\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule enforces setting `SET QUOTED_IDENTIFIER ON`\nnear the top of the file.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nDECLARE @MyVar VARCHAR(30);\nSELECT @MyVar = 'This is incorrect.';\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSET QUOTED_IDENTIFIER ON;\nGO\n\nDECLARE @MyVar VARCHAR(30);\nSELECT @MyVar = 'This is correct.';\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "set-transaction-isolation-level",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL READ UNCOMMITTED Near Top of File",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that the statement SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL READ UNCOMMITTED is placed near the top of a T-SQL file.",
    "explanation" : "# Enforce setting SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL READ UNCOMMITTED near top of file\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule enforces setting `SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL READ UNCOMMITTED` near the top of a file.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nDECLARE @MyVar VARCHAR(30);\nSELECT @MyVar = 'This is incorrect.';\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL READ UNCOMMITTED;\nGO\n\nDECLARE @MyVar VARCHAR(30);\nSELECT @MyVar = 'This is correct.';\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "set-variable",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce setting variable using SELECT statement",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that variables are assigned values using a SELECT statement instead of SET.",
    "explanation" : "# Enforce setting variable with SELECT statement\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule enforces setting variable values\nusing a `SELECT` statement.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nDECLARE @MyVar VARCHAR(30);\nSET @MyVar = 'This is incorrect.';\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nDECLARE @MyVar VARCHAR(30);\nSELECT @MyVar = 'This is correct.';\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 2,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "unicode-string",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Use of Unicode Characters in Non-Unicode Strings",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of Unicode characters in strings declared with non-Unicode data types.",
    "explanation" : "# Disallow use of unicode chars in non-unicode string\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule disallows using unicode characters in\nstrings that do not support unicode characters.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nDECLARE @MyVar VARCHAR(30) = 'Ⱦhis is incorrect.';\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nDECLARE @MyVar NVARCHAR(30) = N'Ⱦhis is correct.';\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "update-where",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce WHERE Clause in UPDATE Statements",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that every UPDATE statement includes a WHERE clause to specify which rows should be updated.",
    "explanation" : "# Enforce use of WHERE condition when using UPDATE\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule enforces the use of a WHERE condition in UPDATE statements.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nUPDATE mytable\nSET CreatedOn = GETDATE()\nFROM dbo.MyTable AS mytable;\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nUPDATE mytable\nSET CreatedOn = GETDATE()\nFROM dbo.MyTable AS mytable\nWHERE CreatedOn IS NULL;\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "upper-lower",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Performance",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Using UPPER or LOWER Functions in Comparisons in Case Insensitive Databases",
    "description" : "This rule disallows the use of UPPER or LOWER functions in WHERE clause comparisons in SELECT statements when the database is case insensitive.",
    "explanation" : "# Disallow using UPPER/LOWER functions in comparisons\n\n## Rule Details\n\nThis rule disallows using `UPPER` or `LOWER` functions\nwhen performing comparisons since this is not required\nin case insensitive databases and can affect query SARGability.\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT user_name\nFROM dbo.MyTable\nWHERE UPPER(first_name) = 'NATHAN';\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsql\nSELECT user_name\nFROM dbo.MyTable\nWHERE first_name = 'NATHAN';\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  }
]